iterations.reply:
I didn't add the metadata fetch. SendReply's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0`, and the spec says that clause is the node's entire authority. Calling `https://metadata.internal.example` would need `http-client`, which this node was not granted. If you want enrichment, the grant has to change first, and I can add it then.

The body below sends the reply and checks the two `ensures` clauses. If the channel reports non-delivery or an empty session, it traps instead of returning a violating confirmation, so the output stays unchanged for every case that satisfies the contract.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{agent-response, delivery-confirmation};

    import aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0;

    export run: func(reply: agent-response) -> delivery-confirmation;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::response_channel;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        // requires: len(text) <= 100000 holds of every input by contract.
        let confirmation = response_channel::send(&reply.text);

        // ensures: delivered == true
        if !confirmation.delivered {
            panic!("delivery not confirmed by response channel");
        }
        // ensures: present(session_id)
        if confirmation.session.is_empty() {
            panic!("response channel returned no session identity");
        }

        confirmation
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

